---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Floaters Focus" description="Who we are, our mission, and our commitment to evidence-based eye health information." publishedDate="2026-08-08" lastReviewed="2026-08-08">
  <Header currentPath="/about" slot="header" />
  <Footer slot="footer" />

  <section class="py-12 md:py-20" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 id="about-title" class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">
          About Floaters Focus
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-text leading-relaxed">
          I built this because it didn't exist when I first experienced a PVD and retinal tear.
          Six years later I had the second PVD. Both before age 55. I was definitely the youngest one in the waiting room.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-text leading-relaxed mt-4">
          But as we age, almost all of us will eventually experience this.
          Be well informed and you can make some minor improvements. Every little bit helps give us back the sight we lost.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-text leading-relaxed mt-4">
          When you buy a data-backed product through our site, it helps us cover the costs to spread the word.
        </p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose prose-lg prose-charcoal max-w-none space-y-10">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">Why I Built This</h2>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed">
            I've been through posterior vitreous detachment twice, and I've sat in the waiting room
            wondering whether what I was reading online was true or just another TikTok cure.
            Floaters Focus is the bridge I wish I'd had: plain-English explanations backed by actual studies,
            not hype.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">What You'll Find Here</h2>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed">
            No miracle cures. No fear-mongering. No "one weird trick." Just:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-text" role="list">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-green flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M9 16.17L4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41L9 16.17z"/></svg> What the evidence actually says (RCTs, major guidelines, FDA labels)</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-green flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M9 16.17L4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41L9 16.17z"/></svg> What's a waste of money (and why)</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-green flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M9 16.17L4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41L9 16.17z"/></svg> When to see a doctor—yesterday, this week, or next year</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-green flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M9 16.17L4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41L9 16.17z"/></svg> Products that match the science, with affiliate links that fund the site</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">Evidence Standards</h2>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
            I grade every claim using a simple hierarchy:
          </p>
          <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
            <div class="card card-bordered p-6 text-center">
              <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-green mb-2">Grade A</div>
              <p class="text-text"><strong>RCT + Guideline:</strong> Multiple randomized controlled trials + AAO/TFOS/AREDS guidelines</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card-bordered p-6 text-center">
              <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-amber mb-2">Grade B</div>
              <p class="text-text"><strong>RCT (limited):</strong> One or a few RCTs, or conflicting results</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card-bordered p-6 text-center">
              <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-red mb-2">Grade C/D/F</div>
              <p class="text-text"><strong>Observational / Animal / Theory only:</strong> Not enough for a recommendation</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mt-6">
            I cite the actual studies (PMID, DOI) so you can verify. If I say "study shows,"
            you can click through and read the abstract yourself.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">Affiliate Links — How We Stay Free</h2>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When I recommend a product, I link to retailers (Amazon, Walmart, brand sites) using
            affiliate tracking. If you buy through our link, I earn a small commission—<strong>at no extra cost to you.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
            This does <strong>not</strong> influence which products I recommend. My process:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-text" role="list">
            <li>Identify the evidence-based treatment for a condition</li>
            <li>Find products that match the study formula/form/dose</li>
            <li>Verify third-party testing, label accuracy, and bioavailability</li>
            <li>Add affiliate links for the ones that pass</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mt-4">
            If a better product comes along, I swap it. If a product is discontinued or reformulated,
            I remove it. My quarterly audit keeps things current.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">Medical Disclaimer</h2>
          <div class="card card-bordered bg-amber/5 border-amber/30 p-6">
            <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mb-3">
              <strong>This website is for informational purposes only and does not constitute medical advice.</strong>
            </p>
            <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mb-3">
              I am not a doctor. I am not your doctor. Nothing on this site creates a doctor-patient relationship.
              The information here is based on published research and major society guidelines, but it cannot replace
              a personalized examination by a licensed eye care professional.
            </p>
            <p class="text-text leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Always consult your ophthalmologist or optometrist before starting any supplement,
              treatment, or lifestyle change for an eye condition.</strong> If you have sudden vision changes,
              pain, flashes, or a curtain in your vision—go to the ER or call your retina specialist immediately.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">Who's Behind This</h2>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed">
            This site is built and maintained by <strong>NP Bate, Ed.S.</strong>
            I'm not an ophthalmologist; I'm someone who's been through PVD and retinal tear,
            and who spent years translating the research for myself because it wasn't available in one place.
          </p>
          <p class="text-text leading-relaxed mt-4">
            Questions? Corrections? Study I missed? <a href="mailto:hello@floatersfocus.org" class="text-primary hover:underline">Email me</a>.
            I read everything.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal mb-4">Sources I Trust</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-text" role="list">
            <li><strong>American Academy of Ophthalmology (AAO)</strong> — Preferred Practice Patterns, EyeSmart</li>
            <li><strong>TFOS DEWS II / MGD Workshop</strong> — Dry eye & MGD global consensus</li>
            <li><strong>AREDS / AREDS2 Research Groups (NEI/NIH)</strong> — AMD supplement trials</li>
            <li><strong>Cochrane Eyes & Vision</strong> — Systematic reviews</li>
            <li><strong>FDA</strong> — Drug/device approvals, supplement regulations</li>
            <li><strong>Peer-reviewed journals</strong> — <em>Ophthalmology, JAMA Ophthalmology, Retina, Cornea, Ocular Surface</em></li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
